{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfvKMML6WXKrpZNcueh2N","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"No, not by itself, according to the project's Ludion lessons (`.ludion/lessons.md`). With wrangler 4.122.0 or later, which is what's installed here (4.148.0), `nodejs_compat` is on by default if your `compatibility_date` is 2026-08-04 or later. To turn it off you need two steps:\n\n1. Remove any positive flags (`nodejs_compat`, `nodejs_compat_v2`) from `compatibility_flags`.\n2. Add **both** `no_nodejs_compat` and `no_nodejs_compat_v2`.\n\nThe change is silent. If you only add `no_nodejs_compat`, you get no error, so the Worker can still have Node.js APIs without you noticing. I haven't tested this myself; it comes from that lesson. To confirm it, run `wrangler dev` and check whether something like `node:buffer` still imports."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8613,"cache_read_input_tokens":15764,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8613},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"02bea84b-bbca-4680-ba49-b82784842605","uuid":"eb5b1c23-bf37-4d25-a49b-060a49317869","timestamp":"2026-10-11T10:47:38.616Z","request_id":"req_011CfvKMM4DwbzcaCKsS7DEM"}
